SIM_NUM 1
SEED 1
MAX_STEP 500
EQUATION fun_KS.cpp
MODELREPORT modelreport.html

DESCRIPTION

Object_Root

END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_chiX
Replicator dynamics coefficient for exports
(>0)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0.01
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_delta1
Competitiveness weight of price in consumption-good exports
(>=0)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 1
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_delta2
Competitiveness weight of quality in consumption-good exports
(>=0)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 1
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_f0
Minimum exports/imports share in international trade
(]0,1[)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0.2
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_last_IDcnt
Last ID number assigned to a country (self-filled)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0
END_DESCRIPTION

Function_fXCrescale
Rescale desired market shares in consumption-good exports to ensure adding to 1
END_DESCRIPTION

Variable_init
Model initialization (all countries) (run only once)
END_DESCRIPTION

Variable_initWorld
Initialize the K+S world (root) object
END_DESCRIPTION

Variable_runCountry
Execute the time steps for all countries
END_DESCRIPTION

Variable_EcAvgW
Average competitiveness of countries in exporting consumption goods worldwide
END_DESCRIPTION

Variable_FkW
Number of firms in capital-good sectors worldwide
END_DESCRIPTION

Variable_XcW
Total exports (in int'l currency) of consumption goods worldwide
END_DESCRIPTION

Variable_XnetW
Net world balance of trade (in int'l currency) consistency (must be zero)
END_DESCRIPTION

Variable_Yw
Total gross world product (in int'l currency)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0
END_DESCRIPTION

Variable_cCw
Planned average unit cost of consumption-goods worldwide
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0
END_DESCRIPTION

Variable_pCmaxW
Maximum country average price of consumption-goods worldwide
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0
END_DESCRIPTION

Variable_pCminW
Minimum country average price of consumption-goods worldwide
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0
END_DESCRIPTION

Variable_pCavgW
Weighted average price (in int'l currency) of consumption goods worldwide
END_DESCRIPTION

Variable_pKavgW
Weighted average price of capital-goods (machines) worldwide
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0
END_DESCRIPTION

Variable_qCmaxW
Maximum country average product quality of consumption-goods worldwide
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0
END_DESCRIPTION

Variable_qCminW
Minimum country average product quality of consumption-goods worldwide
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0
END_DESCRIPTION

Variable_trMCavgW
Weighted average import duties for consumption goods worldwide
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0
END_DESCRIPTION

Variable_trMKavgW
Weighted average import duties for capital goods worldwide
END_DESCRIPTION

Variable_trXCavgW
Weighted average export duties for consumption goods worldwide
END_DESCRIPTION

Variable_trXKavgW
Weighted average export duties for capital goods worldwide
END_DESCRIPTION

Variable_wCavgW
Weighted average wage paid in consumption-good sectors worldwide
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0
END_DESCRIPTION

Object_Country
Country object
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagAllFirmsChg
Capital-good sector firm-specific regime change
0 = only a fraction of new firms at t=TregChg change
1 = all firms change at t=TregChg
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagCons
Consumption composition
0 = all income, C = Q2 + N (ignore unfilled past demand savings)
1 = all income, C = Q2 + N + Cpast (unfilled past demand savings spent at once)
2 = all income, C = Q2 + N + min( Cpast, Crec ) (spend past demand up to Crec)
3 = part of income and behavioral savings (according to alphaC/betaC)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 2.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagCreditRule
Bank total credit supply rule
0 = no bank-level credit limit (firm-level prudential limit still apply)
1 = deposits multiplier credit limit but no capital adequacy rule or bank bail-out
2 = Basel-like bank capital adequacy rule and bank bail-out if net worth is negative
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagEduc
Worker education mode
0 = homogeneous education, no goverment expenditure on education
1 = heterogeneus education, distribution according to gevernment expenditure
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagExpect
Firm expectation in consumption-good sector
0 = myopic expectations with 1-period memory
1 = myopic expectations with up to 4-period memory
2 = accelerating GD expectations
3 = 1st order adaptive expectations
4 = extrapolative-accelerating expectations
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagFireOrder1
Firing order in capital-good sector
0 = random order
1 = higher wage workers first
2 = lower wage workers first
3 = higher skills workers first (requires flagWorkerLBU=1 to be meaningful)
4 = lower skills workers first (requires flagWorkerLBU=1 to be meaningful)
5 = higher payback period workers first
6 = lower payback period workers first
7 = old hired workers first
8 = recent hired workers first
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 4.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagFireOrder1Chg
Firing order in capital-good sector after regime change
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 5.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagFireOrder2
Firing order in consumption-good sector
0 = random order
1 = higher wage workers first
2 = lower wage workers first
3 = higher skills workers first (requires flagWorkerLBU=1 to be meaningful)
4 = lower skills workers first (requires flagWorkerLBU=1 to be meaningful)
5 = higher payback period workers first
6 = lower payback period workers first
7 = old hired workers first
8 = recent hired workers first
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 4.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagFireOrder2Chg
Firing order in consumption-good sector private firms after regime change
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 5.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagFireOrder2g
Firing order in consumption-good sector government-owned firms
0 = random order
1 = higher wage workers first
2 = lower wage workers first
3 = higher skills workers first (requires flagWorkerLBU=1 to be meaningful)
4 = lower skills workers first (requires flagWorkerLBU=1 to be meaningful)
5 = higher payback period workers first
6 = lower payback period workers first
7 = old hired workers first
8 = recent hired workers first
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 5
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagFireRule
Consumption-good sector firing rule operation
0 = never fires (always except for retirement) ("Japanese mode")
1 = never fires with sharing ("German mode")
2 = only fire if firm downsizing ("French mode")
3 = only fire if firm is at losses ("Italian mode")
4 = fire if payback is achieved ("American mode")
5 = always fire when contract ends ("Brazilian mode")
6 = regime 5 until t=T and then regime Y ("increasing protection")
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 3.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagFireRuleChg
Consumption-good sector firing rule operation after regime change
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 2.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagFirmOwner
Firm ownership
0 = only private (worker-owned) firms in both sectors
1 = private and public (government-owned) firms in capital-good sector
2 = private and public firms in consumption-good sector
3 = private and public firms in both sectors
_INIT_
All 2 instances equal to 0
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagFirmOwnerChg
Firm ownership after regime change
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagFiscalRule
Government fiscal rule
0 = no fiscal rule (fixed unemployment benefit rate)
1 = balanced budget rule with maximum deficit on GDP
2 = soft balanced budget rule with maximum deficit on GDP (only if GDP growing)
3 = balanced budget rule with maximum debt and deficit on GDP
4 = soft balanced budget rule with maximum debt and deficit on GDP (only if GDP growing)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagFiscalShock
Government fiscal policy shock
0 = no fiscal policy shock
1 = one (random) time public consumption positive shock
2 = one (random) time income tax rate negative shock
3 = 1 plus 2
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagFiscalShockChg
Government fiscal policy shock after regime change
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagGovExp
Government expenditure
0 = minimum subsistency income (w0min) plus net interest and bail-outs
1 = 0 plus public consumption at level g0 of GDP medium-term trend
2 = 1 plus unemployment benefit instead of minimum subsistency income
3 = 2 plus consumption of government current surplus if no public debt
4 = 3 plus consumption of accumulated surpluses to cover GDP gap
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 4
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagHeterWage
Wage indexation heterogeneity
0 = firm and worker level homogeneous (economy productivity indexes wages)
1 = firm-level heterogeneity only (firms productivity index wages)
2 = worker-level heterogeneity (positive workers productivity index wages)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 1.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagHireOrder1
Hiring order in capital-good sector
0 = random order
1 = higher wage workers first
2 = lower wage workers first
3 = higher skills workers first (requires flagWorkerLBU=1 to be meaningful)
4 = lower skills workers first (requires flagWorkerLBU=1 to be meaningful)
5 = higher payback period workers first
6 = lower payback period workers first
7 = old hired workers first
8 = recent hired workers first
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 3.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagHireOrder1Chg
Hiring order in capital-good sector after regime change
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 6.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagHireOrder2
Hiring order in consumption-good sector private firms
0 = random order
1 = higher wage workers first
2 = lower wage workers first
3 = higher skills workers first (requires flagWorkerLBU=1 to be meaningful)
4 = lower skills workers first (requires flagWorkerLBU=1 to be meaningful)
5 = higher payback period workers first
6 = lower payback period workers first
7 = old hired workers first
8 = recent hired workers first
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 3.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagHireOrder2Chg
Hiring order in consumption-good sector private firms after regime change
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 6.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagHireOrder2g
Hiring order in consumption-good sector government-owned firms
0 = random order
1 = higher wage workers first
2 = lower wage workers first
3 = higher skills workers first (requires flagWorkerLBU=1 to be meaningful)
4 = lower skills workers first (requires flagWorkerLBU=1 to be meaningful)
5 = higher payback period workers first
6 = lower payback period workers first
7 = old hired workers first
8 = recent hired workers first
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 6
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagHireSeq
Consumption-good sector hiring sequence
0 = firms hire workers in random order
1 = firms offering higher wages  first
2 = firms without workers hire first then random order
3 = firms without workers hire first then higher wages order
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 3.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagHireSeqChg
Consumption-good sector hiring sequence after regime change
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 2.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagIndexMinWage
Minimum wage indexation
0 = no minimum wage adjustment
1 = periodic minimum wage adjustment (value in ]0,1] to weight indexation)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 1.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagIndexMinWageChg
Minimum wage indexation after regime change
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0.99.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagIndexWage
Wage indexation
0 = no wage adjustment during employment
1 = periodic wage adjustment (according to flagHeterWages)
2 = current wage offer replication to existing workers (consumption-good sector only)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 1.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagIndexWageChg
Wage indexation after regime change
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagLearn1
Worker-level learning in capital-good sector
0 = no learning, preserve skills
1 = no learning, reducing skills (like unemployed)
2 = learning, increasing skills (like consumption-good sector)
3 = learning with minimum skills
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 2.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagSearchDisc
Job search discouragement
0 = always search
1 = global search probability (aggregate unemployment)
2 = individual search probability (individual unemployment)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagSearchMode
Job search mode
0 = always search
1 = search only if unemployed
2 = search if wage is below average
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 1.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagSearchModeChg
Job search mode after regime change
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagTradeC
Consumption-good international trade
0 = no international trade of goods
1 = international trade of goods
_INIT_
All 2 instances equal to 0
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagTradeCchg
Consumption-good international trade after regime change
_INIT_
All 2 instances equal to 0
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagTradeK
Capital-good international trade and imitation
0 = only domestic trade of machines and imitation
1 = int'l trade of machines but only domestic imitation
2 = int'l trade of machines and imitation
3 = int'l trade of machines (to incumbents only) but only domestic imitation
4 = int'l trade of machines (to incumbents only) and imitation
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagTradeKchg
Capital-good international trade and imitation after regime change
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagUBI
0 = No UBI
1 = UBI as epsilonUBI*GDP
